<span class="k">static</span> <span class="kt">void</span> <span class="nf">cleanupAfterMain</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="p">{</span>
    <span class="n">printf</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"5. main() 返回后自动调用</span><span class="se">\n</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="p">}</span>

<span class="n">__attribute__</span><span class="p">((</span><span class="n">destructor</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">101</span><span class="p">)))</span>
<span class="k">static</span> <span class="kt">void</span> <span class="nf">earlyCleanup</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="p">{</span>
    <span class="n">printf</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"4. 优先级 101 的析构先跑</span><span class="se">\n</span><span class="s">"</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
<span class="c1">// Output order: after main ends → 4 → 5</span>
<span class="c1">// Note: the larger the destructor priority number, the earlier it runs (the opposite of constructor!)</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p><strong>Common pitfalls</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">abort()</code> / <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">_exit()</code> don’t trigger destructors</li>
  <li>Destruction order is the reverse of construction order</li>
  <li>Destructors may race during multithreaded exit, so try not to take locks inside them</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="23-cleanup--automatically-called-when-a-variable-leaves-scope">2.3 <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cleanup</code> — automatically called when a variable leaves scope</h3>

