<h3 id="115-the-swift-compilers-use-of-swift_name">11.5 The Swift compiler’s use of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">swift_name</code></h3>

<p>The Swift compiler automatically generates <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">swift_name</code> attributes for every <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@objc</code> class, ensuring the Swift-side API follows Swift naming conventions. You can see many auto-generated <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">__attribute__((swift_name(...)))</code> in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">.swiftinterface</code> files.</p>

